{{Quote|I am calling it the Specter Particle. As my Archimedians explain, mimicry is in its nature. An echo. Exposed to precept circuits, we are able to imprint behaviors! Like an infant mirroring her surrogate. Only this infant can set the world on fire.|[[Parvos Granum]], inventor of Specter technology}}
<section begin="intro" />
A '''Specter''' is an AI-controlled [[Allies|ally unit]] that will fight alongside a player for the duration of a mission. They have their own set of weapons and/or abilities that they can use against enemies and are generally summoned via a consumable [[Equipment#Gears|Gear]] item.
<section end="intro" />
{{tocright}}
==Lore & History==
{{Main|The Deadlock Protocol}}

=== Specter Particle Theory ===
Specters were first developed by {{Faction|Corpus}} Founder, '''[[Parvos Granum]]''', spearheaded by his creation of the '''Specter Particle Theory'''; an idea of a unique type of particle that, when exposed to preset data, can be imprinted with mimicked behaviors.<ref>''"Parvos Granum originated the Specter Particle Theory? Guts. This old coot is a whole order of intelligence, and that's bad for us."'' - '''[[The Business]]''', during [[The Deadlock Protocol]].</ref> To accelerate development, Parvos would go on to steal a undisclosed sample from the {{Faction|Entrati}}, stating that they, ''"kept their secrets long enough."''<ref>''"Some doors ought to remain closed? That's not in my world view. Fire. Fusion. Void. Progress always comes entangled with risk, with violence. With the precious sample obtained, development is accelerating. The [[Entrati]] have kept their secrets long enough."'' - '''Parvos Granum''' during [[The Deadlock Protocol]].</ref> Additionally, Parvos would then use this sample to bait the {{Faction|Orokin}} into raiding his labs, who sent a Warframe assault team as a result. Due to the site being heavily rigged with explosives however, both the labs and the Warframes were all vaporized.

The {{Weapon|Xoris}}, presumably designed by Parvos Granum,<ref>''"Nef's given us a cipher for an old Granum file. "Phantasmic Scintilla and Motive Forces." We'll need more specifics to build whatever this tool is."'' - [[The Business]].</ref> is linked to Specter technology,<ref>''"An obscure glaive weapon of Corpus provenance, intrinsically linked to Specter technology. The Xoris strikes rapidly and with great devastation. It is capable of chaining combos infinitely."'' - Xoris weapon description.</ref> as it contains a unique energy trap that allows it to contain Specter Particles to amplify the explosion of its mid-flight detonation.<ref>''"A weapon? Glaive-class but with an energy trap... Specter Particles, maybe? Has a mid-flight detonation trigger. Tricky, but I'm sure you'll get the hang of it. Gear up and lets go."'' - [[The Business]]</ref>

After Parvos's attempted assassination, his guardian Warframe, {{WF|Protea}}, would use her temporal abilities to preserve him within a [[Granum Void|region of the Void]], resulting in her sacrifice,<ref>''"-When the Board's assassins overloaded my transport's Void drive, [[Protea]]... my beautiful Protea... and her gift for manipulating time... preserved me.-But at the cost of all that she was. Now she is nothing more than a Specter of her former self. My beautiful Protea."'' - [[Parvos Granum]]</ref> and presumably becoming a [[Protea Specter|Specter]] as a result.<ref>''"The victim and beneficiary of Parvos Granum's research into Specter Particle Theory, this is all that remains of the Protea Warframe who sacrificed herself to keep Granum safe in a pocket realm beyond time."'' - '''[[Protea Specter|Protea Specter's]]''' [[Codex]] entry.</ref>

After Parvos's tomb is discovered, [[Nef Anyo]] entrust his [[Treasurer]]s with safekeeping his {{Resource|Granum Crown}} tributes; these units will fervently defend their crowns from any wayward thief, including the {{Faction|Tenno}}. If not dispatched quickly, the Treasurer will teleport to the [[Void]],<ref>''"Fulfill your Desire and others will follow. I follow Parvos. To freedom!"'' - '''[[Treasurer/Quotes|Treasurer Quotes]]'''</ref> and presumably become an [[Errant Specter]].<ref>''"The ghostly minions of Parvos Granum within his timeless prison-realm."'' - Errant Specter Codex entry.</ref>

=== Composition & Construction ===
When defeated, Errant Specters will release a mass of '''Specter Particles''', which can be absorbed by other Errant Specters to increase their strength. If fully discharged of energy, these particles will become piles of inert dust, referred to as {{Resource|Spectral Debris}}. If reenergized, this dust can also be used when creating various robotic tech.
