==Gameplay==
===Enemy===
{{Main|Specter (Enemy)}}
[[Specter (Enemy)|Enemy Specters]] are primarily encountered as guardians of the [[Origin System]]'s [[Solar Rail]] [[Junctions]], and must be defeated to unlock connections to new planets and destinations on the [[Star Chart]]. Specter-like enemy Warframes also serve as enemies during specific [[Quest]]s.

===Ally===
{{Main|Specter (Tenno)}}
[[Warframe]] Specters can act as allies or enemies depending on the circumstances. As allies, [[Specter (Tenno)|Specters]] are AI-Controlled Warframe-replicants employing customizable load-outs (which are configured via the [[Foundry]]). They can be summoned via consumable [[Gear]] wheel items in all [[Mission]]s, except [[Archwing]] and [[Sanctuary Onslaught]].

Warframe Specters come in 4 tiers (Vapor, Phase, Force and Cosmic). Their blueprints be acquired by completing [[Rescue]] missions, with higher-level missions rewarding high-tier Specters.

Some Specters can also be generated by Warframes are weapon abilities, like with {{WF|Wukong}}'s {{A|Celestial Twin}} and the {{Weapon|Ballistica Prime}} charged shot.

==Syndicate Specters==
Access to Syndicate Specters can be acquired by taking allegiance to the desired [[Syndicate]]s and attaining the first tier in their ranks. Syndicate Specters can be purchased by spending {{sc|2,500}} for a bundle of five. Only one instance for each type of Specters can be summoned. Summoning another one while an identical Specter is active will kill the one already out.

Their blueprints can also be acquired from Syndicate death squads, with the type of blueprint awarded depending on their respective Syndicates.

