*'''Volatile Ancient Protector''' grants 90% [[Damage Redirection]] and 100% stagger/knockdown resistance to all allied units within 15m, denoted with a soft green glow on said units when in range. It can also knockdown enemies with a frontal {{D|Blast}} wave. Ancient Protectors will naturally follow where players head towards, and will melee attack enemy units that gets close by.
*'''Venomous Charger''' will rush ahead and fight independently of where the player heads towards, and will usually melee assault enemies point blank, passively inflicting them {{D|Toxin}} damage from its Eximus Venomous aura. Due to its sub-optimal AI behavior as well as their tendency to rush towards to melee enemy units, they die quickly and is considered the least useful of the six syndicate specters.
*'''Arson Corrupted Lancer''' will fight independent of where the player heads towards, and can cast its Eximus {{D|Heat}} blast ability that will knockdown all enemies that gets caught within line-of-sight of the unit.
*'''Arctic MOA''' will passively slow down nearby enemies with its {{D|Cold}} eximus aura, and deploys ice globe to protect everyone inside, even from enemy crowd control. It fights independently of where the player heads towards, and the allied ice globe cannot be shot through.
* '''Energy Leech Roller''' will cast energy leech aura on enemies, which on hit inflicts them with {{D|Magnetic}} status, and grants all allied units nearby an energy regen worth 3 energy / second over 3 seconds, totaling 9 energy restored every hit. Energy regen from multiple hits does not stack. The roller will naturally follow wherever the player heads towards, preferring to stay close and grant its player passive energy regeneration where it can.
*'''Shock Shield Osprey''' will provide additional +25% maximum shield to all applicable allied units nearby, and upon being in range will instantly restore the shields of said unit. It will passively follow allied units though not necessarily following the player character. It very rarely uses its autoturret to fight back as well as use its homing Eximus {{D|Electricity}} bolts to attack.

