===Stalker===
{{Main|Stalker}}
[[File:Stalker_Thumb.png|right|100x100px]]
The '''Stalker Specter Blueprint''' was a reward from [[Nightwave]]'s [[Nightwave/Nora's Mix Volume 7|Nora's Mix Volume 7]] and returned as a reward in [[Operation: Belly of the Beast]]. Unlike other specters, the Stalker blueprint has infinite uses. He is cloned from the pre-[[The Second Dream]] Stalker, not the ones players can pilot in [[Duviri]]. 

Unlike Tenno Specters, the Stalker Specter will prioritize fighting enemies rather than following the player similar to most Syndicate Specters. This makes it a bad choice for missions that involve the player moving to different locations as the Stalker will not follow nor teleport, and even in missions that remain in one room, the Stalker may funnel enemies to a point away from an objective (e.g. [[Defense]]). However, should the Stalker Specter lose all health, he can be revived.

Possesses the abilities {{A|Smoke Screen}}, {{A|Shuriken}}, {{A|Absorb}}, and {{A|Pull}}.{{Clr}}

